    <statement><p>Find the equation of the parabola with the given properties</p>
<p>Focus <m>(5,0)</m>, directrix <m>x=-5</m>.</p>
<p><fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0001"/><m>=x</m></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\frac{y^{2}}{20}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><m>x</m>-axis rather than on the
<m>y</m>-axis and the directrix is a vertical line rather than horizontal as in the parabola in standard position. 

 
Therefore,  the equation of the parabola is obtained by interchanging <m>x</m> and <m>y</m> in
<m>y=\frac{1}{4c}{x}^{2}</m>. 

 
Also,  by the given information
<m>c=5</m>. Hence,
<me>x=\frac{1}{4c}{y}^{2}=\frac{1}{4\cdot 5}{y}^{2}</me> or
<me>x=\frac{{y}^{2}}{20}</me>


</solution>
